course: dictionary
lesson: 7493
title: Words about the post
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Postal means to do with the post, which is another word for mail: the letters and parcels that are sent and delivered. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it for clues. «Postal workers and sorting machines read addresses in that order.» Sorting machines and addresses tell you the sentence is about letters and parcels, so postal workers must be the people who send and deliver them.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «The Mongol empire ran a postal system.» If you swap in «mail system», the sentence still makes sense, so postal means to do with the post. A system is an organised way of doing something, so a postal system is the way letters are carried from place to place.
explain: Some words are used in everyday life in different countries. A postal code helps sort post. In the UK it is called a postcode, and in the USA it is called a ZIP code. The words are different, but the job is the same.
fact: Postal means to do with the post, or mail.
fact: A postal worker is a person who sends and delivers letters and parcels.
fact: A postal address shows where a letter should go.
fact: A postal code is a group of letters and numbers that helps sort post. It is called a postcode in the UK and a ZIP code in the USA.
exercise: In «postal workers», what does postal mean? | To do with the sea: boats and waves | Very loud and noisy | * To do with the post: sending and delivering letters | To do with sport: running and jumping
exercise: What is a postal address for? | To show the score in a game | To show how to cook rice | To show how old a person is | * To show where a letter should go
exercise: What is a postal code called in the USA? | Postcode | Post box | Stamp | * ZIP code
test: Ella says a postal worker is a person who fixes cars. Is she right? | Yes, they fix cars at the garage | No, they only work at night | Yes, they teach children in school | * No, postal workers send and deliver letters and parcels
test: What does a postal vote mean? | A vote for the best cake at the fair | A vote shouted out in the street | A vote made on the phone only | * A vote sent in by post
exam: Which is a postal service? | * A service that carries letters and parcels between towns | A church service on Sunday | A tennis match between two players | A service that cleans windows at school
